{"user": "Why do corners matter so much? White got a1 and h1 and it felt like I couldn't ever flip those back.", "user_ts": "2026-08-14T21:09:36.798903+00:00", "assistant": "Exactly \u2014 **corners matter because once a disc is in a corner, it can never be flipped back.**\n\nTo flip a disc, it has to be **sandwiched between two enemy discs** in a straight line. But a corner has no square \u201cbehind\u201d it, so it can\u2019t be sandwiched.\n\nSo when White got **a1** and **h1**, those became **permanent White discs**. Even more, they help \u201canchor\u201d nearby edge discs, making whole edges harder to flip.\n\nThat\u2019s why squares next to empty corners are dangerous: playing near the corner can let the opponent take it next move.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-14T21:09:36.798903+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-14T21:09:41.798903+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 2, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 0.6666666666666666, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "votes": {"General Principle": 3, "Local Justification": 2, "Positive Feedback": 1}, "confidence": {"General Principle": 1.0, "Local Justification": 0.6666666666666666, "Positive Feedback": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["General Principle"], "llama": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "sonnet": ["Local Justification", "General Principle", "Positive Feedback"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "ne