{"user": "Do you only count discs at the very end? I thought I was doing okay in the middle but then everything flipped on me.", "user_ts": "2026-08-14T21:09:51.798903+00:00", "assistant": "Yes \u2014 **only the final disc count matters**.\n\nIn the middle, having lots of discs can be misleading because many of them are still **flippable**. What often matters more is:\n\n- **Corners**: permanent, can\u2019t be flipped.\n- **Edges anchored by corners**: often become safe.\n- **Mobility**: leaving your opponent few good/legal moves.\n- **Endgame parity/counting**: who gets the last flips.\n\nFor this board, it\u2019s full, so the game is over:\n\n- **Black: 21**\n- **White: 43**\n\nWhite wins by **22**.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-14T21:09:51.798903+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-14T21:09:56.798903+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 3, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 1.0, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Positive Feedback": 1}, "confidence": {"Board Report": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0, "Positive Feedback": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "sonnet": ["Board Report", "General Principle", "Positive Feedback"], "llama": ["Board Report", "General Principle"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse": ["Direct Instruction"]}}
{"user": "What does 'mobility' mean here? Just how many legal moves you have?", "user_ts": "2026-08-14T21:10:06.798903+00:00", "assistant": "Yes \u2014 **mobility** mainly means **how many legal moves you have**, but also **how good those moves are**.\n\nHigh mobility = you have choices.  \nLow mobility = you may be forced to play bad squares, like next to a corner.\n\nIn endgames, mobility is huge because if one player has **no legal move**, they must **pass**, and the other player may get extra moves in a row.\n\nHere, though, the board is full: **0 empty squares**, so there are no moves and mobility no longer matters \u2014 it\u2019s just final count.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-14T21:10:06.798903+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-14T21:10:11.798903+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 1, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 0.3333333333333333, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Local Justification": 1, "Positive Feedback": 1}, "confidence": {"Board Report": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0, "Local Justification": 0.3333333333333333, "Positive Feedback": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "llama": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "sonnet": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle", "Positive Feedback"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse": ["Direct Instruction"]}}
